---
source: crates/rustman-cli/src/tests.rs
expression: help
---
Discover and plan probes without sending any request (a dry run)

Usage: rustman explore plan [OPTIONS] --spec <SOURCE> --target <URL>

Options:
      --spec <SOURCE>
          The OpenAPI document: a file path or an http(s) URL

      --target <URL>
          The base URL probes are sent to; its origin is the only one allowed

      --probes <LIST>
          Probe families, comma-separated (default: all but bola): conformance, auth, negative-input, method-not-allowed, lifecycle, bola, fuzz, undocumented-status, error-leakage, security-headers

      --operations <GLOB>
          Only operations matching a glob over operationId, path or "METHOD /path" (repeatable)

      --seed <U64>
          Seed of the fuzz cases (default: random, printed with the plan)

      --fuzz-cases <N>
          At most this many fuzz cases per operation
          
          [default: 50]

      --allow-mutations
          Also allow POST, PUT and PATCH

      --allow-destructive
          Also allow DELETE (implies --allow-mutations; never against production)

      --allow-host <ORIGIN>
          Allow another origin, scheme://host[:port] (repeatable)

      --production <HOST>
          Confirm a production target by repeating its exact host

      --identity-b <ENV>
          The environment of a second identity, for bola probes

      --allow-remote-refs
          Fetch $refs to other http(s) documents instead of refusing them

      --env <NAME>
          Environment (default: RUSTMAN_ENV, then default_environment)

      --workspace <DIR>
          Workspace directory (default: search from the current directory upwards)

      --graph
          Also print the resource graph (producers of each path parameter)

      --json
          Print the plan as JSON

      --color <WHEN>
          Color: auto (a terminal without NO_COLOR or TERM=dumb), always or never
          
          [default: auto]

  -v, --verbose...
          Log more on stderr: -v requests, -vv headers, -vvv everything (RUST_LOG, when set, replaces these levels)

  -h, --help
          Print help
